// Division by zero is 0, and so is the remainder -- it used to be a SIGFPE on
// the host and a fault on a board, taking the whole runtime down because one
// rule divided by a parameter nobody had set. INT_MIN / -1 traps the same way
// on x86; it wraps, as + and * do.
#variable Z = 0
#variable M = -2147483647
#variable Q = 0
#variable R = 0
#variable W = 0
#variable F float = 0.0
Q = 7 / Z
R = 7 % Z
W = (M - 1) / -1
F = 2.5 / (Z * 1.0)
